#* {{quote-web
|en
|date=08 April 2024
|author=Ching-en Chiou
|title=Taiwan’s hospital completes medical assistance to Saint Kitts and Nevis
|work=w:Radio Taiwan International
|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/qDu8u
|archivedate=May 04, 2024
|url=https://en.rti.org.tw/news/view/id/2010968
|text=The Taipei Veterans General Hospital (TVGH) announced in a press release on Monday that its medical team participated in the 2024 Lesser Antilles Medical Assistance Team (LAMAT) in '''Saint Kitts and Nevis''' this March, embarking on a 10-day mission to provide community medical services at the local hospital. The hospital stated that this cross-national medical cooperation has proven successful and received high praise.{{...}}<br>Taiwan's ambassador to '''Saint Kitts and Nevis''', Michel Lin ({{lang|zh|林昭宏}}), expressed gratitude for TVGH's contributions to diplomatic relations. He emphasized that the medical mission has significantly bolstered medical cooperation between the two nations, establishing a strong foundation for expanded collaboration across various fields in the future.}}

